{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>For he is to him a son of old age.</b> And if you ask: is not Binyamin a son of old age? One may answer: Binyamin's love is not bound in Yaakov's heart like his love for Yosef, because when his mother bore him she died." "<b>Pasim.</b> After the name of his sale — retrospectively. Another interpretation: a term of appeasement, like a deed of appeasement; a fine garment, to appease him."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:36.887547374Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}